## 3. Optimized Solution — Greedy + Three Pointers

```python
class Solution:
    def maxEqualSum(self, s1: list[int], s2: list[int], s3: list[int]) -> int:
        n1 = len(s1)
        n2 = len(s2)
        n3 = len(s3)

        top1 = 0
        top2 = 0
        top3 = 0

        sum1 = sum(s1)
        sum2 = sum(s2)
        sum3 = sum(s3)

        while top1 < n1 and top2 < n2 and top3 < n3:
            if sum1 == sum2 == sum3:
                return sum1

            if sum1 >= sum2 and sum1 >= sum3:
                sum1 -= s1[top1]
                top1 += 1

            elif sum2 >= sum1 and sum2 >= sum3:
                sum2 -= s2[top2]
                top2 += 1

            else:
                sum3 -= s3[top3]
                top3 += 1

        return 0
```

**Time Complexity:** O(n1 + n2 + n3)  
**Space Complexity:** O(1)

